---
alwaysApply: true
---
Use multi-stage Docker builds to separate dependencies, build artifacts, and runtime.

Set resource limits (mem_limit, cpus) in docker-compose for each service.

Define all services (frontend, backend, db) in a single docker-compose.yml.

Use .dockerignore to keep builds clean and fast.

Set up proper volumes for hot reload in development (volumes: in compose).

Use healthchecks for services to ensure proper startup (healthcheck: in compose).

Keep environment variables in .env, never hardcoded.

Use named networks in docker-compose to isolate app traffic.

Keep production images minimal (no dev tools), using node:alpine or similar.

For deployment, use .env.production, build with --target=production, and use docker secrets or a secret manager for sensitive data.